MicroLink v2 (https://github.com/CamM2325/microlink) commit 1cb8d1c8a8408ad1b9a339b18bed3e970b71dafe, MIT
(components/microlink/ of that commit; nothing else from the repository)
headboard-led local patches:
- ml_derp.c: send to a peer through the peer's home DERP region (up to ML_DERP_MAX_ALT=1 extra
  connection, opened on demand, read like the home connection (also waited on in the idle
  select()), closed after 60 s idle; only when enough memory is free (>= 96 KB PSRAM with
  CONFIG_MBEDTLS_EXTERNAL_MEM_ALLOC, which headboard sets), otherwise the home connection is used
  as before). Upstream only connects to its own home region, so peers homed elsewhere (e.g. a
  Home Assistant on a US VM, region 10, while we are in Tokyo, region 7) were unreachable without
  a direct UDP path. ml_derp_tx_item_t has a region field, ml_derp_conn_t has
  region/last_used_ms/retry_after_ms; the TLS helpers take the connection (ml_derp_conn_t *)
  instead of microlink_t, and ml_derp_connect() is derp_conn_open() on the home connection
- microlink.c: initialise the extra connections' sockets to -1, and unblock them on stop
